"""Domain enums of this service, one module per domain.

An enum lives in ``core/enums/<domain>.py`` (``core/enums/orders.py``)
and is re-exported here, so the rest of the project imports it from the
package: ``from src.core.enums import OrderStatusEnum``.

Every enum subclasses ``BaseStrEnum`` and its name ends in ``Enum``
(``OrderStatusEnum``); ``tempest check`` reports one without the suffix
(``ENUM001``). The database type drops one trailing ``Enum``, so the
suffix never changes a migration.
"""

__all__: list[str] = []
